WEBVTT

00:16.080 --> 00:20.080
He's done it yet again,
another absurd stuff.

00:24.750 --> 00:26.510
Unbelievable.

00:26.510 --> 00:29.050
Not only did that slime
become a Demon Lord,

00:29.050 --> 00:31.090
but he also defeated the Saint Hinata.

00:31.440 --> 00:33.300
You're being disrespectful, Vaughn.

00:33.300 --> 00:36.850
Still, you're telling me to seriously
believe what's written here?

00:37.410 --> 00:38.890
There is no mistake.

00:39.390 --> 00:42.090
Over a hundred Crusaders
were utterly defeated,

00:42.090 --> 00:45.530
and Demon Lord Rimuru defeated
the Saint Hinata in a one-on-one battle.

00:46.190 --> 00:51.010
As a result, Lubelius is establishing
a diplomatic relationship with Tempest.

00:51.930 --> 00:54.830
Don't be so mad, Henrietta.

00:54.830 --> 00:57.000
I am as surprised by this
as anyone here.

00:57.000 --> 01:00.040
I am sure Vaughn couldn't help but laugh.

01:00.580 --> 01:03.130
But now is not the time to laugh.

01:04.500 --> 01:05.880
King Gazel.

01:05.880 --> 01:10.130
Demon Lord Rimuru may have
grown stronger than you are now.

01:10.690 --> 01:12.890
He's a threat.

01:13.550 --> 01:14.850
Lady Jaine!

01:14.850 --> 01:17.810
It is threatening that he has
evolved into a Demon Lord,

01:17.810 --> 01:20.640
but I know what kind
of man Rimuru is.

01:20.640 --> 01:23.560
I doubt he would
betray my trust in him.

01:34.320 --> 01:36.240
What is your bidding, my liege?

01:38.700 --> 01:41.750
A ceremony to mark his
appointment as a Demon Lord?

01:41.750 --> 01:47.000
That Rimuru...
Just what is he planning this time?

03:16.970 --> 03:19.970
EPISODE 61: THE NATIONS AND INVITATIONS

03:19.970 --> 03:21.970
EPISODE 61: THE NATIONS AND INVITATIONS
Hmm...

03:22.380 --> 03:23.870
Does something matter?

03:23.870 --> 03:26.570
I'm just thinking we need
something other than festivals

03:26.570 --> 03:32.360
like a hit event that would encourage people
to keep coming back to our nation.

03:33.480 --> 03:36.610
I asked Mjöllmile about
the battle tournament,

03:36.610 --> 03:39.990
but I don't think we can hold it
that many times in a year.

03:39.990 --> 03:45.040
So I want something that can get
people coming on a daily basis.

03:45.040 --> 03:46.160
I see...

03:46.160 --> 03:49.130
Oh, c'mon! Don't be such a hard-head!

03:49.130 --> 03:50.880
It's rowdy over there.

03:50.880 --> 03:52.500
Did something happen?

03:53.130 --> 03:58.010
Like I said!
We're taking over this place!

03:58.010 --> 04:02.760
I get what you're trying to say,
but we can't easily accept that, you know?

04:03.350 --> 04:05.020
This guy is Gobukyuu.

04:05.020 --> 04:07.850
He is Myrd's apprentice,
and a skilled craftsman.

04:07.850 --> 04:13.020
I'll go ask Great Rimuru, so I'd like it
if you could stay put and wait here.

04:13.020 --> 04:13.900
No!

04:13.900 --> 04:17.530
We came all the way here after
abandoning our last labyrinth!

04:18.530 --> 04:24.910
Are you going to kick out us poor,
homeless women with no place else to go?

04:25.580 --> 04:29.500
Still, this is Great Rimuru's territory.

04:29.500 --> 04:32.340
Tch, can't sob story my way in, eh?

04:32.340 --> 04:35.050
In that case,
I won't hesitate to use force!

04:35.590 --> 04:39.260
If you keep nitpicking every little thing,

04:39.260 --> 04:41.260
my sweet Beretta here won't stay—

04:41.260 --> 04:43.100
What are you doing here?

04:46.100 --> 04:49.250
W-Well, hey, Rimuru!
How is it going?

04:49.980 --> 04:51.400
Lady Ramiris.

04:51.730 --> 04:54.420
I've brought over some new wood.

04:54.420 --> 04:57.410
What are you doing, Ms. Treyni?

04:58.030 --> 05:01.160
W-Well, if it isn't Sir Rimuru.
I'm glad to see you well.

05:01.160 --> 05:04.160
- Crap!
- Could you explain this to me, Ms. Treyni?

05:04.160 --> 05:07.410
W-Well, this is not what it looks like.

05:07.410 --> 05:11.170
L-Lady Ramiris did nothing wrong,
um...

05:11.170 --> 05:13.210
Explain to me, Beretta.

05:13.210 --> 05:15.670
Ah, so it has to be me, huh?

05:16.840 --> 05:18.440
It all began yesterday...

05:20.510 --> 05:22.550
I don't think we can keep this on anymore.

05:22.990 --> 05:25.430
We need to move out of here, too!

05:25.430 --> 05:27.430
Correct as always, Lady Ramiris!

05:27.430 --> 05:29.310
You always have the most brilliant idea!

05:29.310 --> 05:30.560
I know, right? Right?

05:30.560 --> 05:31.890
One moment, please.

05:32.900 --> 05:36.150
Setting aside whether it is
a brilliant idea or not,

05:36.150 --> 05:38.940
where do you intend us to move to?

05:38.940 --> 05:41.400
And could you tell us why?

05:41.740 --> 05:43.780
I'm glad you asked!

05:43.780 --> 05:46.410
Beretta, don't you think it's boring here?

05:46.410 --> 05:50.960
There's nothing to play with in here,
and the only fun we have is making golems.

05:50.960 --> 05:52.670
Barely anyone even comes.

05:53.250 --> 05:56.750
But there are a lot of things in Tempest!

05:56.750 --> 06:01.390
So I'm thinking
we should move out there!

06:02.450 --> 06:04.220
But Lady Ramiris,

06:04.220 --> 06:07.310
didn't Sir Rimuru already
turn you down once?

06:07.310 --> 06:11.140
Beretta, you're thinking
too hard about this.

06:11.140 --> 06:13.350
Sir Rimuru is a nice man.

06:13.350 --> 06:18.320
He'd never deny a request from someone
as cute and lovable as Lady Ramiris!

06:19.840 --> 06:25.070
This dryad is a capable woman
only when Lady Ramiris is not involved...

06:25.740 --> 06:27.450
So that's the story.

06:27.450 --> 06:29.330
Beretta, you traitor!

06:29.830 --> 06:33.540
And as a matter of fact,
like Lady Ramiris said,

06:33.540 --> 06:37.460
we came here after she had
sealed all the doors to her labyrinth.

06:37.460 --> 06:38.960
There you have it!

06:38.960 --> 06:43.840
So if you kick me out of here,
I would have nowhere else to live!

06:43.840 --> 06:45.970
Oh, poor, poor Lady Ramiris.

06:45.970 --> 06:49.330
Please don't pamper her
like that, Ms. Treyni.

06:49.330 --> 06:51.930
But well, I get your situation.

06:52.630 --> 06:54.850
Sorry that you went through that,
Gobukyuu.

06:54.850 --> 06:57.440
Well, I was fine, but...

06:57.900 --> 07:00.570
She got some of our guards...

07:00.570 --> 07:01.400
Hey!

07:02.320 --> 07:05.070
W-Well, I got a little excited...

07:05.070 --> 07:07.370
It's not Lady Ramiris's fault!

07:07.370 --> 07:10.490
Those guards were saying
mean things to her,

07:10.490 --> 07:13.580
so I simply put them
to sleep with my spell.

07:14.080 --> 07:15.710
So to sum it up...

07:15.710 --> 07:17.580
You tried to build a hut here

07:17.580 --> 07:19.460
and the guards tried to stop you.

07:19.460 --> 07:23.670
And since they got in your way,
you ordered Ms. Treyni to put them to sleep,

07:23.670 --> 07:25.840
but you got found by Gobukyuu.

07:25.840 --> 07:27.590
Do I have this right?

07:27.920 --> 07:29.360
Well...

07:29.360 --> 07:31.310
No, that's not exactly the case!

07:31.310 --> 07:34.600
Or so I think... or I don't think...

07:34.600 --> 07:35.690
Maybe?

07:35.690 --> 07:37.530
Oh, you...

07:45.530 --> 07:46.650
Door...

07:48.910 --> 07:51.280
Doors to the labyrinth, huh...

07:52.370 --> 07:54.290
Maybe this could work.

07:56.790 --> 08:00.960
SORCEROUS DYNASTY THALION

08:16.230 --> 08:17.310
Your Excellency.

08:17.310 --> 08:21.990
I have received an invitation
from the nation of monsters.

08:23.070 --> 08:26.940
I never expected he would actually
get recognized as a Demon Lord...

08:26.940 --> 08:29.160
Well, that's fine and all...

08:29.860 --> 08:33.990
I can't really bring Her Excellency
with me this time...

08:39.330 --> 08:41.080
Oh?

08:42.210 --> 08:43.090
Your Excellency?

08:43.440 --> 08:47.550
You went to such
an interesting place all by yourself?

08:47.550 --> 08:51.590
Well, weren't you fortunate?
I'm sure you had a fabulous time there.

08:51.590 --> 08:52.600
Ah...

08:52.600 --> 08:55.170
Not only that, you went there
claiming to be my envoy

08:55.170 --> 08:57.650
and formed a relationship with them
without me knowing.

08:57.650 --> 09:02.350
If our business with them were so important,
I would love to go there myself.

09:02.350 --> 09:04.520
M-My pardon, Your Excellency!

09:04.520 --> 09:06.610
It was undoubtedly a nation of monsters!

09:06.610 --> 09:10.110
I couldn't possibly bring you along
into such a dangerous place!

09:10.510 --> 09:15.370
If such an interesting creature exist,
I would love to see it with my own eyes.

09:15.370 --> 09:19.040
Even more, to meet a Demon Lord
so soon after his birth?

09:19.040 --> 09:23.330
I've lived for many years,
but not even I had such an opportunity.

09:23.700 --> 09:26.590
Have you heard of the phrase
"steal a march"?

09:28.170 --> 09:30.840
To be treated this way
by my own people...

09:30.840 --> 09:34.090
What a pitiful emperor I am!

09:34.720 --> 09:36.720
I've never been so envio— No,

09:36.720 --> 09:39.270
so offended in my life!

09:39.270 --> 09:43.940
Who knows just how much excite—
I mean, danger that awaits there,

09:43.940 --> 09:46.110
but you went off there without telling me!

09:48.570 --> 09:50.750
It is scandalous!

09:54.410 --> 09:57.060
So, what do you intend to do with this?

09:58.330 --> 10:01.130
Do what, Your Excellency?

10:01.130 --> 10:03.670
Mmm? You want to play dumb?

10:04.250 --> 10:06.040
By the way, Erald.

10:06.040 --> 10:09.340
You know those sweet pastries
we procured from Mr. Yoshida?

10:09.340 --> 10:12.760
It appears their quality
has drastically improved recently.

10:13.320 --> 10:15.500
You know why?

10:15.500 --> 10:17.350
Mr. Yoshida?

10:17.350 --> 10:22.560
I believe he was the baker who runs
an establishment in Engrassia.

10:22.560 --> 10:23.730
What about him?

10:23.730 --> 10:25.900
I suppose even a strategic
genius such as yourself

10:25.900 --> 10:27.890
is oblivious to
the goings-on in the streets?

10:27.890 --> 10:28.980
What a disappointment.

10:28.980 --> 10:30.780
I'm terribly sorry.

10:31.440 --> 10:36.530
So what does Mr. Yoshida have to do
with this invitation from Sir Rimuru?

10:36.530 --> 10:39.870
What? You really don't know?

10:39.870 --> 10:44.330
Eryune brought some of his pastries
to me as a souvenir a while back...

10:44.330 --> 10:46.540
...but it seems she didn't give you any.

10:46.540 --> 10:49.550
She what?!

10:52.090 --> 10:54.840
Well then, let me tell you.

10:54.840 --> 10:59.470
Mr. Yoshida has started to procure
his ingredients from a certain source.

10:59.470 --> 11:02.470
And thanks to that,
the quality of his pastries improved.

11:02.470 --> 11:07.520
The souvenir Eryune brought me was
the most tremendous cake I've ever had.

11:07.520 --> 11:09.110
A cake?!

11:09.110 --> 11:12.570
Why didn't you bring
anything for me, Eryune?!

11:12.570 --> 11:17.990
So I scouted him
to come work here in Thalion.

11:17.990 --> 11:19.990
But he turned me down.

11:19.990 --> 11:24.370
No matter how much money I offered him,
he refused to come here.

11:24.750 --> 11:28.000
What are you doing, Your Excellency?

11:30.500 --> 11:35.700
But recently, Mr. Yoshida apparently
said he'd be closing his café.

11:35.700 --> 11:39.430
Is he planning to open another location?
Or maybe he's planning to move elsewhere?

11:40.010 --> 11:43.470
Either way, being unable
to taste his desserts during

11:43.470 --> 11:46.560
his hiatus would be
a huge problem, wouldn't it?

11:46.560 --> 11:49.020
Not really, no.

11:49.770 --> 11:51.190
Oh?

11:51.190 --> 11:54.030
You're really saying that?

11:54.030 --> 11:57.400
Eryune is quite fond of
that café's sweets,

11:57.400 --> 11:59.910
so if she could get
easy access to those,

11:59.910 --> 12:03.160
I believe she would come
back home more often.

12:04.500 --> 12:09.000
As a matter of fact, she often comes
back here for our regular tea parties.

12:10.880 --> 12:12.290
Those two!

12:12.290 --> 12:15.880
Even though I told them to report to me
whenever Eryune comes back home!

12:16.880 --> 12:19.390
This is a grave news, is it not?!

12:19.790 --> 12:20.830
Yes, it is.

12:21.350 --> 12:24.890
But using my authority and funds,

12:24.890 --> 12:27.390
I've obtained some rather
interesting information.

12:29.190 --> 12:30.600
Let me hear it.

12:31.540 --> 12:32.970
What a surprise!

12:32.970 --> 12:35.280
The place said to be
where Mr. Yoshida's moving to

12:35.280 --> 12:37.820
is none other than the nation
you visited, Tempest!

12:37.820 --> 12:38.490
What?!

12:38.930 --> 12:42.830
Tell me, what were you doing over there?

12:48.250 --> 12:50.500
That's incredible, Shuna!

12:50.880 --> 12:54.250
You perfectly replicate that new recipe!

12:59.200 --> 13:02.970
Ah... So that recipe that she meant...

13:02.970 --> 13:04.260
...was Mr. Yoshida's...

13:04.610 --> 13:08.000
Are you sure your supposed
"brilliant mind" still works normally?

13:08.000 --> 13:10.100
I am sorry...

13:10.100 --> 13:16.280
I was under the impression you went there
to monopolize the sweets for Eryune.

13:16.280 --> 13:19.110
Not even I would go that far.

13:19.110 --> 13:20.450
I wouldn't doubt it.

13:20.450 --> 13:22.570
You always go crazy for your daughter.

13:24.830 --> 13:26.620
So, Your Excellency.

13:26.620 --> 13:31.000
If I may return to the topic,
how will we respond to Sir Rimuru?

13:31.500 --> 13:32.790
Let's see..

13:33.960 --> 13:36.340
The destination is a nation of monsters...

13:36.340 --> 13:40.220
That means I'll be opening
myself up for scrutiny

13:40.220 --> 13:43.760
by those seeking
to get one up on me.

13:43.760 --> 13:46.470
Not only that, there's no guarantee
that no one would

13:46.470 --> 13:49.770
try to use this opportunity
to take down Her Excellency.

13:49.770 --> 13:52.310
You worry too much, Erald.

13:54.190 --> 13:55.310
Your Excellency?

13:56.230 --> 13:59.280
No matter what those youngsters think,

13:59.280 --> 14:02.570
none could ever exact revenge against me.

14:04.770 --> 14:09.080
That Demon Lord Rimuru is the one
we cannot let our guard down against.

14:17.950 --> 14:20.960
What do you mean?

14:22.840 --> 14:27.470
Rimuru easily accepted to build
the highway to Thalion, didn't he?

14:27.470 --> 14:28.850
Yes.

14:28.850 --> 14:33.730
He asked for rights to things
like tolls and customs fees,

14:33.730 --> 14:36.360
but he'll do the entire
construction job on his end.

14:36.360 --> 14:37.260
That's the issue.

14:38.130 --> 14:42.150
Those rights are a source
of a massive fortune.

14:42.150 --> 14:45.740
Can't you see that looking at me, Erald?

14:46.320 --> 14:49.490
You mean rights to revenue sources?

14:49.490 --> 14:52.200
You still have a long way to go, huh.

14:52.200 --> 14:59.250
Long-lived races such as ourselves
make plans based on long-term profit.

14:59.250 --> 15:00.880
Of course.

15:00.880 --> 15:06.050
I decided after comparing the tolls
of the highway Demon Lord Rimuru made

15:06.050 --> 15:11.770
versus the cost it would take for us
to build the highway ourselves.

15:11.770 --> 15:13.640
How naive of you.

15:13.640 --> 15:16.850
Building a highway through
that forest is a daunting task,

15:16.850 --> 15:20.860
and nobody has tried to before
because there was no benefit to doing so.

15:21.530 --> 15:27.740
But now, the vast Southern Demon Lord
domains are ruled by Demon Lord Milim.

15:27.740 --> 15:31.370
They're set to be a prosperous land
with all the military might they boast.

15:31.910 --> 15:34.660
Then, we have the Western Nations
to the northwest

15:34.660 --> 15:37.040
and the Armed Nation of Dwargon
to the north.

15:37.710 --> 15:43.880
And the new nation, Tempest,
is nestled right between them, is it not?

15:43.880 --> 15:47.510
Hence why I decided that instead of
taking on the highway construction,

15:47.510 --> 15:51.140
it was better to secure profits
through payment of their usage fees.

15:51.140 --> 15:53.970
Normally that would be a job well done.

15:53.970 --> 15:58.230
But we're dealing with a long-lived race,
and a Demon Lord at that.

15:58.230 --> 16:03.650
You should think much more carefully
when signing an agreement with no time limit.

16:03.980 --> 16:05.900
That's why you got
eight points out of ten.

16:07.400 --> 16:10.880
We should've lent a hand
in the construction effort.

16:10.880 --> 16:14.040
If we had at least a record of
cooperating with the construction,

16:14.040 --> 16:17.380
that would have made our
fee negotiation much easier.

16:18.920 --> 16:21.380
Wh-What have I done?!

16:21.380 --> 16:23.170
I failed to read that far ahead!

16:23.530 --> 16:25.340
The tides are changing.

16:25.340 --> 16:27.720
Being able to notice that
is good and all,

16:27.720 --> 16:30.680
but you can't keep on being held
by your own preconceptions.

16:31.680 --> 16:35.430
Anyway, about my response
to the invitation, right?

16:36.560 --> 16:41.690
Between the sweets shop
and the highway...

16:41.690 --> 16:45.440
This Demon Lord Rimuru
is well-versed in human society.

16:46.230 --> 16:50.200
There's no doubt
that he's a former Otherworlder,

16:50.200 --> 16:54.660
but he now possesses the power to fully
utilize that knowledge and experience.

16:55.160 --> 16:59.210
Demon Lord or not,
he's truly extraordinary.

16:59.790 --> 17:04.500
Hero Shizue Izawa's disciple,
Grandmaster Yuuki Kagurazaka,

17:04.500 --> 17:07.380
and the Captain of the Crusaders
Hinata Sakaguchi

17:07.380 --> 17:09.930
are all important figures
in the Western Nations,

17:09.930 --> 17:13.220
but their influence is below that of
Demon Lord Rimuru, which means...

17:13.720 --> 17:15.560
Which means...?

17:16.930 --> 17:19.230
We can't afford not to attend this.

17:33.660 --> 17:35.530
E-Erm...

17:35.530 --> 17:38.660
What is going to, er, happen to us?

17:39.010 --> 17:41.670
You don't have to be all polite.

17:41.670 --> 17:45.040
Also, if that's your attempt at being polite,
then you're failing miserably.

17:45.040 --> 17:46.170
Ehe!

17:46.710 --> 17:51.530
Gobukyuu, I'm thinking of making a space
for evacuation under the arena.

17:51.530 --> 17:52.630
Would that be possible?

17:53.800 --> 17:58.180
Even if we construct the building
with our executives' strengths in mind,

17:58.180 --> 18:01.180
the space right under
the building won't be safe.

18:01.180 --> 18:05.310
If there's a space under,
the shock waves could cause a cave-in.

18:05.900 --> 18:09.320
But I think it won't be an issue
if we move this space a little.

18:09.700 --> 18:11.240
I see.

18:11.240 --> 18:13.820
I'd like to build a door down there.

18:15.070 --> 18:16.580
A door, sir?

18:16.580 --> 18:17.620
Yeah.

18:17.620 --> 18:22.210
Make it thick and heavy, like you put
a bunch of stone tablets around it.

18:22.210 --> 18:26.590
Are you planning to make
an evacuation space beyond that door?

18:26.590 --> 18:28.630
No, that wouldn't be needed.

18:28.630 --> 18:30.630
What's important is the door itself.

18:30.630 --> 18:32.090
Isn't that right, Ramiris?

18:32.460 --> 18:36.800
R-Rimuru? Are you...
Are you saying that...

18:37.170 --> 18:42.060
I want to make an underground labyrinth—
A dungeon, with your power.

18:47.520 --> 18:51.230
Then we place monsters in there
and have Adventurers fight them.

18:51.230 --> 18:55.320
I think we can attract quite a number
of people every day with that.

18:55.670 --> 18:59.330
A-A labyrinth?
Right below the arena?

18:59.690 --> 19:03.610
We're going to use the arena
to train the rookies,

19:03.610 --> 19:06.330
and we're also planning to have
a potion shop on the premises.

19:06.730 --> 19:09.450
And if we can have Ramiris
run the dungeon for us,

19:09.450 --> 19:11.800
I bet taverns for Adventurers
looking for a quick drink

19:11.800 --> 19:14.380
on the way back from work
would be a big hit.

19:14.380 --> 19:16.390
Me? You want me to run it for you?

19:16.720 --> 19:19.220
We'll get profits from the Adventurers

19:19.220 --> 19:21.470
and you will get
a place to live and a job.

19:21.470 --> 19:24.890
Furthermore, I'll give you some
spending money, too.

19:24.890 --> 19:27.900
S-So you mean that...

19:27.900 --> 19:31.320
Not only I could build
a labyrinth and live here,

19:31.320 --> 19:34.860
but you will also give me
a full-fledged job?!

19:34.860 --> 19:37.910
If you accept my offer, of course.

19:38.700 --> 19:41.580
Okay, okay, then that means...

19:41.580 --> 19:45.040
I can finally escape from being called
a "jobless shut-in"?

19:45.390 --> 19:48.270
I'm so glad for you, Lady Ramiris!

19:50.340 --> 19:56.470
U-Um, so did you really mean
that you will give me an allowance, too?

19:56.470 --> 19:58.050
Yes, I'm serious.

19:58.050 --> 20:01.970
But I don't know how much profit
we will get until we get things going.

20:02.370 --> 20:07.230
How about twenty percent of the profits
after I deduct all the expenses?

20:07.230 --> 20:10.730
H-How much do you think
it would add up to?

20:11.140 --> 20:15.190
Let's see, assuming we get around
a thousand Adventurers coming every day,

20:15.190 --> 20:17.550
your share will be around two gold coins.

20:17.550 --> 20:18.740
How does that sound?

20:18.740 --> 20:22.740
Wh-What?! I can get that much, sir?!

20:23.080 --> 20:26.960
But that's still just an estimate,
and there's no guarantee it'll work out.

20:26.960 --> 20:29.750
There's no point in it
if nobody was coming, after all.

20:29.750 --> 20:35.240
But if you wish to live here anyway,
I don't think it's a bad deal for you.

20:37.510 --> 20:41.680
I'm gonna be filthy rich now!

20:41.680 --> 20:47.270
Now nobody will get to call me
a deadbeat and a destitute Demon Lord!

20:47.270 --> 20:50.270
I can see how she got picked on
about that often...

20:50.270 --> 20:54.070
Hey, we still need to discuss
where we should build the arena,

20:54.070 --> 20:55.860
so come back here.

20:58.900 --> 21:02.740
So I am thinking of expanding
the open area outside the western gate,

21:02.740 --> 21:05.160
where the highway ended
and open the arena there.

21:05.590 --> 21:08.910
Why, though?
Didn't you have space within the town?

21:08.910 --> 21:13.100
We're housing the Lycanthrope
refugees there right now.

21:13.100 --> 21:15.570
We have streets of temporary
housing laid out for them,

21:15.570 --> 21:18.420
so we can't build an arena over that.

21:18.810 --> 21:22.840
We can't throw the Lycanthropes
out of town, too.

21:22.840 --> 21:25.510
I think development there
will have to wait until after

21:25.510 --> 21:27.930
Sir Geld completes work on
the new Eurazanian capital.

21:27.930 --> 21:32.690
Then how about we have them
move to my labyrinth?

21:32.690 --> 21:37.030
I can transport the whole area in one go,
so it won't be much of a hassle.

21:37.530 --> 21:38.390
Huh?

21:40.490 --> 21:44.820
Y-You mean you can move
the inhabitants there, too?

21:45.230 --> 21:46.700
Um, so...

21:46.700 --> 21:51.150
I must first get their permission before
I can transport them to the labyrinth.

21:51.150 --> 21:54.920
I can transport any inanimate
objects with no problem!

21:54.920 --> 21:56.500
Seriously?!

21:56.500 --> 22:00.260
So you can move all
the Lycanthropes' houses

22:00.260 --> 22:03.930
and belongings inside your labyrinth
anytime you want?

22:03.930 --> 22:06.390
Yup! That's right!

22:06.390 --> 22:08.010
That's amazing.

22:08.010 --> 22:12.290
To be frank, I thought you
didn't have any useful abilities.

22:12.940 --> 22:14.730
Th-That's so mean!

22:14.730 --> 22:17.860
How could you say that to me, a woman
said to be the strongest Demon Lord—

22:17.860 --> 22:21.150
There, there.
No need to be so mad, Ramiris.

22:21.150 --> 22:24.570
More importantly,
tell me what else you can do!

22:27.980 --> 22:29.580
Wonderful!

22:29.580 --> 22:33.250
That solves our safety concerns!

22:33.250 --> 22:35.130
That's wonderful, Ramiris!

22:35.520 --> 22:37.540
Really?! You mean it?!

22:38.080 --> 22:40.630
I really am great, aren't I?

22:40.630 --> 22:41.840
Yup!

22:41.840 --> 22:45.210
Our ambitions are as good as accomplished!

22:45.680 --> 22:47.970
I'm counting on you, Ramiris!

22:47.970 --> 22:51.310
Yes! You can count on me!

22:53.980 --> 22:56.980
It'll be nothing but smooth sailing ahead!

22:59.980 --> 23:01.940
A smooth sailing, huh...

23:01.940 --> 23:04.910
Let's just hope the ship
isn't made out of mud.

24:36.000 --> 24:39.540
Next time,
"The Labyrinth and The Storm Dragon."
